// ============================================================================
// ENTERPRISE POWER BI ANALYTICS PORTFOLIO — DAX MEASURE LIBRARY
// Section: 05 Regions (Geographic Analytics)
// Author: Datta Sable (https://dattasable.com)
// Source: Datta_Sable_PowerBI_DAX_Visuals_Implementation_Handbook.xlsx & PRD Section 6.5
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
// Measure Name: Region Sales Share %
// Purpose: Calculate regional contribution percentage against total filtered sales.
// Business Definition: Share of total sales generated by the selected geographic region.
// Expected Data Type: Percentage
// Formatting: 0.0%
// Required Tables: fact_orders_2023
// Required Columns: fact_orders_2023[Region], fact_orders_2023[Sales_Amount_USD]
// Filter Context Behavior: Uses ALLSELECTED on Region so that selecting categories or dates recalculates the relative regional contribution.
// Recommended Visuals: Donut Chart, 100% Stacked Bar Chart, Matrix, Filled Map tooltip.
// Validation Method: Sum of Region Sales Share % across all visible regions equals 100.0%.
// Known Limitations: Relies on orders table Region column.
// ============================================================================
Region Sales Share % = 
DIVIDE ( [Total Sales], CALCULATE ( [Total Sales], ALLSELECTED ( fact_orders_2023[Region] ) ) )

// ============================================================================
// Measure Name: Regional Sales
// Purpose: Explicit measure for regional sales revenue.
// Business Definition: Total sales revenue within the active regional filter context.
// Expected Data Type: Currency
// Formatting: $#,##0.00
// Required Tables: fact_orders_2023
// Required Columns: fact_orders_2023[Sales_Amount_USD], fact_orders_2023[Region]
// Filter Context Behavior: Respects slicers on Continent, Country, Region, and Date.
// Recommended Visuals: Shape Map, Filled Map, Clustered Bar Chart.
// Validation Method: Total matches [Total Sales] ($12,840,570.00).
// Known Limitations: Single-year baseline.
// ============================================================================
Regional Sales = 
CALCULATE ( [Total Sales] )

// ============================================================================
// Measure Name: Regional Profit
// Purpose: Explicit measure for regional operating profit.
// Business Definition: Total operating profit within the active geographic boundary.
// Expected Data Type: Currency
// Formatting: $#,##0.00
// Required Tables: fact_orders_2023
// Required Columns: fact_orders_2023[Profit_Amount_USD], fact_orders_2023[Region]
// Filter Context Behavior: Evaluates profit dynamically across geographic dimensions.
// Recommended Visuals: Map Bubble Size, Bar Chart, Matrix.
// Validation Method: Total matches [Total Profit] ($2,310,910.00).
// Known Limitations: Overhead costs are not allocated regionally; based on order-level cost.
// ============================================================================
Regional Profit = 
CALCULATE ( [Total Profit] )

// ============================================================================
// Measure Name: Regional Profit Margin %
// Purpose: Evaluates regional profitability efficiency.
// Business Definition: Ratio of regional operating profit to regional sales.
// Expected Data Type: Percentage
// Formatting: 0.0%
// Required Tables: fact_orders_2023
// Required Columns: fact_orders_2023[Sales_Amount_USD], fact_orders_2023[Profit_Amount_USD]
// Filter Context Behavior: Divides regional profit by regional sales.
// Recommended Visuals: Heatmap Matrix, Map Color Saturation, KPI Card.
// Validation Method: Regional margins vary around the 18.0% portfolio average.
// Known Limitations: Excludes regional distribution center overhead.
// ============================================================================
Regional Profit Margin % = 
DIVIDE ( [Regional Profit], [Regional Sales], 0 )

// ============================================================================
// Measure Name: Regional Sales Rank
// Purpose: Rank geographic regions by total revenue generated.
// Business Definition: Ordinal ranking (1 to N) of regions by sales volume.
// Expected Data Type: Integer
// Formatting: #,##0
// Required Tables: fact_orders_2023
// Required Columns: fact_orders_2023[Region]
// Filter Context Behavior: Evaluates over ALLSELECTED(fact_orders_2023[Region]).
// Recommended Visuals: Regional Leaderboard, Table visual.
// Validation Method: North America ranks #1 ($4,846,210), followed by Europe ($3,108,550).
// Known Limitations: Ties broken by standard RANKX dense ranking rules.
// ============================================================================
Regional Sales Rank = 
IF (
    HASONEVALUE ( fact_orders_2023[Region] ),
    RANKX (
        ALLSELECTED ( fact_orders_2023[Region] ),
        [Total Sales],
        ,
        DESC,
        DENSE
    )
)
